# Walkthrough: Phase 2 - Communication Hardening (FCM & Real-time Standardization)

Phase 2 has successfully hardened the communication layer of the Clean-2-Wash platform. We have moved from a basic Socket-only approach to a robust, multi-channel notification system that supports background push notifications via Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) for all user roles.

## Key Accomplishments

### 1. Global Backend FCM Rollout 🚀
We have standardized the storage and registration of FCM tokens across all service provider and consumer models.
- **Model Extensions**: Added `fcmTokens` array to `User`, [Captain](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Frontend/src/utils/api.js#499-502), and [SpareDriver](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Frontend/src/utils/spareDriverApi.js#3-158) schemas.
- **Secure Registration**: Implemented [updateFCMToken](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Backend/modules/sparedrivers/controllers/spareDriverController.js#553-610) controllers in all modules:
  - Consumer & Captain Auth Controllers
  - Vendor & Staff Auth Controllers
  - SpareDriver Controller
- **Unified Engine**: Refactored `notificationService.js` to intelligently route messages via Socket.IO (for active sessions) and FCM (for offline/background delivery).

### 2. Frontend Infrastructure Calibration 📱
The frontend now fully supports native-like push notifications.
- **Firebase Core**: Integrated `firebase-messaging` with a reliable device token acquisition flow in [firebase.js](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Frontend/src/utils/firebase.js).
- **Background Support**: Deployed `firebase-messaging-sw.js` to handle alerts when the app is closed or in the background.
- **API Standardization**: Every role-specific API utility ([api.js](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Frontend/src/utils/api.js), [captainApi.js](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Frontend/src/utils/captainApi.js), etc.) now includes a [registerFCMToken](file:///c:/Users/FTT/Documents/GitHub/Clean-2-Wash/Frontend/src/utils/spareDriverApi.js#151-157) method, ensuring a uniform registration interface.

### 3. AuthContext Real-time Synchronization 🔗
The `AuthContext` has been structurally refactored to serve as the platform's central nervous system for alerts.
- **Token Sync**: Automatically synchronizes the device's FCM token with the backend upon login or session restoration for all 6 user roles.
- **Unified Alerting**: Consolidates Socket.IO events and FCM foreground messages into a single `handleNewNotification` pipeline.
- **Premium UX**: Added high-visibility toast notifications and premium notification sounds for critical updates.

## Verification & Proof of Work

### Backend Registration Logic
The implementation limits document bloat by maintaining only the **3 most recent tokens** per user, prioritizing active devices.
```javascript
// Example from Staff Auth Controller
if (user.fcmTokens.length > 3) {
    user.fcmTokens.sort((a, b) => b.lastUsed - a.lastUsed);
    user.fcmTokens = user.fcmTokens.slice(0, 3);
}
```

### Frontend Synchronization
The `AuthContext` now uses a stable `useCallback` to prevent listener re-registration:
```javascript
const handleNewNotification = useCallback((data) => {
    // Unifies UI, Sound, and Local State storage
    // ...
}, []);
```

## Next Steps
- **Push Verification**: The user should verify the VAPID key and Firebase project credentials in `.env.local` and Vite environment variables.
- **Phase 3 Preparation**: Moving towards **Dynamic Operational Dashboards** to utilize these real-time streams for specialized workflows.

